# **NimStudio**

**A localhost-first AI chat workspace for NVIDIA APIs.**

Organize conversations into projects, manage multiple API keys, and maintain long-running context through a hybrid memory system — all while keeping your data stored entirely on your local machine.

## **✨ Features**

* **NVIDIA API Integration** — Connect directly to NVIDIA-hosted models.  
* **Project-Based Organization** — Separate your conversations by project/workspace.  
* **One API Key Per Project** — Isolate workflows and usage tracking.  
* **Hybrid Memory System** — Summary memory \+ recent conversation window to prevent context overflow.  
* **Global Rules** — Apply custom system instructions to every conversation automatically.  
* **Real-Time Streaming** — Fast, token-by-token UI responses.  
* **Local SQLite Storage** — Conversations, settings, and memory stay strictly on your hardware.  
* **Open Source & Self-Hosted** — No telemetry. No cloud sync. No vendor lock-in.

## **🎯 Philosophy**

**Simple, Fast, and Private.**

NimStudio is not trying to be a complex agentic framework. There is no forced cloud syncing and no proprietary data harvesting. It is simply a highly responsive, local chat interface built for developers who want better conversation organization and memory management while using top-tier NVIDIA models.

## **🛠️ Tech Stack**

| Layer | Technology | Purpose |
| :---- | :---- | :---- |
| **Frontend** | Next.js, React, Tailwind CSS | UI, Routing, and Styling |
| **State** | Zustand, TanStack Query | Client state and data fetching |
| **Backend** | Hono, TypeScript | API Routes and LLM Streaming |
| **Database** | SQLite, Drizzle ORM | Local-first data persistence |

## **🚀 Quick Start**

### **Prerequisites**

* [Node.js](https://nodejs.org/) (v18 or higher)  
* [pnpm](https://pnpm.io/) package manager

### **Installation**

1. **Clone the repository:**  
   git clone \[https://github.com/aftababu/NimStudio.git\](https://github.com/aftababu/NimStudio.git)  
   cd NimStudio

2. **Install dependencies:**  
   pnpm install

3. **Initialize the local database:**  
   *(This uses Drizzle to create your local SQLite database file)*  
   pnpm db:push

4. **Start the development server:**  
   pnpm dev

5. **Open the workspace:**  
   Navigate to http://localhost:3000 in your browser.

## **📖 Usage Guide**

### **1️⃣ Add an API Key**

By default, NimStudio creates a **Default** project for you. To start chatting, you need to provide an NVIDIA API key.

1. Go to **Settings → API Keys**.  
2. Select your project and paste your NVIDIA API key.

**Need a key?** Visit [build.nvidia.com](https://build.nvidia.com), create a free account, and generate a key from your profile settings.

### **2️⃣ Add a Model**

NimStudio lets you dynamically add models from the NVIDIA registry.

1. Navigate to **Models → Add Model**.  
2. Enter the exact NVIDIA model ID.

**Example Model IDs:**

* meta/llama3-70b-instruct  
* nvidia/nemotron-4-340b-instruct  
* mistralai/mixtral-8x22b-instruct-v0.1

### **3️⃣ Create a New Project (Optional)**

Projects act as isolated workspaces. Each project gets its own API key and conversation history.

1. Go to **Settings → Projects** and create a new project (e.g., "Research", "Work").  
2. Go to **Settings → API Keys** and assign a specific key to that new project.  
3. Switch between projects seamlessly using the top-nav dropdown or the sidebar.

📂 Workspace Structure Example

Default Project  
 ├── System Design Chat  
 └── Bug Fixing Chat

Research Project (Different API Key)  
 ├── Literature Review  
 └── Data Analysis

## **🔒 Security & Local Data**

All application data is stored locally on your machine.

* Conversations & Memory Summaries  
* Global Rules & Model Registries  
* API Keys (Stored locally, encrypted)

**NimStudio does not send your data anywhere except directly to the NVIDIA API endpoint you configure.**

